  - build.yml runs weekly Mondays 04:00 UTC ✓ "weekly CI job builds OpenMS from source at that pin, applies the patches and runs the end-to-end suite" ✓.

  - Q2 detail: version_ AND verboseVersion_ both set (lines 1660-1661). Constructor comment explains. So the CHANGELOG claim "the tool reports its own version (--help, the ini version parameter and the output's software entry used to carry the OpenMS version)" — the source supports this. Good. But note: TOPPBase official=false — ToolHandler. One risk: OpenMS's `--help` prints version; ini writes version param; when reading an ini written by an older version... Actually also: checkIniValidity? TOPPBase compares ini "version" against tool version and warns if different — with old inis carrying OpenMS version "3.5.0-pre..." users get a warning. Minor.

