  35. Q2: version_ = "2.0.0". Risks:
     - TOPPBase ini handling: when writing an ini, the "version" param = 2.0.0; when loading an old ini (with OpenMS version string), TOPPBase warns version mismatch — acceptable, and arguably desirable.
     - OpenMS "official tools" checks: ToolHandler — they pass official=false ✓ handled (the comment says the old name was "passing itself off as an official TOPP tool").
     - mzML software entry: downstream tools (e.g., OpenMS FileInfo, IDMapper) don't validate versions; psi-ms may want name+version — fine.
     - One subtle risk: some OpenMS tools refuse to read ini files whose version is newer than their own; not relevant.
     - Another: verboseVersion_ set ✓ (they handled it).
     - Also OpenMS's `-test` mode / TOPPBase writeParamMetaInfo_ — uses version_ for the software userParam. Fine.
     - Potential real issue: OpenMS 3.6.0-pre version check in CMake? No.
     - Conclusion: low risk; the pair assignment covers --help and ini; residual risks: external workflow parsers expecting OpenMS-style version strings, and any OpenMS internal that parses version_ as x.y.z — "2.0.0" parses fine.

