26:| **Memory** | **~57 GB peak** on a 30-minute gradient and **~170–190 GB** on a 2-hour acquisition at the shipped defaults (the 30–60 min cohort spanned 68–109 GB before the memory work); it scales with the acquisition |
27:| Disk | mzML output is roughly 9 GB for a 30-minute run and 19–20 GB for a 2-hour run at the previous emission; the current default emits 30–70% more spectra. mzPeak is about a third of that |
92:| `-threads` | all cores | worker threads; an explicit `-threads 1` is honoured. Parallelism is isolation windows × flight-time bands, and the window loop reaches ~78× (30-min) to ~89× (2-hour) thread occupancy at 100 threads; window concurrency is bounded by a free-RAM admission gate, not by core count |
100:| `-perf:stream_load` | `true` | read the `.d` frame by frame. `false` holds the whole run in memory (90 GB floor) **and changes the output**: measured, it is slightly *more* sensitive on a large file (+2.0% Sage peptides at unchanged entrapment FDR) for 1.75× the memory and ~1.7× the wall |
101:| `-perf:ms1_trace_bands` | 48 | band-parallel MS1 mass-trace detection (exact partition with a halo). Raised from 12 on 2026-09-07: MS1 tracing 2× faster, peptide sets within 0.06–2% on both engines and both gate datasets; 1 = off |
134:| window-loop occupancy | 78× | 89× |
